Description: Fits single-season occupancy models that correct for false
    positives from automated detectors, such as acoustic classifiers, using
    the multiple-methods (site-confirmation) design of Miller et al. (2011)
    <doi:10.1890/10-1396.1>, in which a subset of detections is verified.
    Models are written in 'Stan' and fitted through 'cmdstanr'. The
    false-positive rate can be constant or depend on site covariates, and
    the true-detection process accepts observation covariates and a recorder
    random effect. The package also simulates data under homogeneous,
    unstructured, and structured false-positive regimes and runs
    simulation-based calibration checks, so users can ask whether the
    correction keeps nominal interval coverage for their own design and how
    much verification it needs.
